{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1454425-crafting-a-vehicle-wonder","id":1454425,"title":"Crafting a Vehicle-Wonder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-06T23:17:38-07:00","id":1454425,"title":"Crafting a Vehicle-Wonder","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> One of my players wants to make an electricity-fueled airplane (chronicle set in the 1910s) with, I suppose, other magic effects bound to it.<br /> <br /> Could it be an <b>Artifact</b> (meaning only awakened people could operate it and she would need <b>Prime 3</b>)? <br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> Is it necessary for that thing to be a <b>Talisman </b>(meaning it needs to have its own Arete and she would need <b>Prime 4</b>)? <br /> <br /> Besides the &quot;own Arete&quot; fact, is there another difference between artifacts and talismans in terms of power?<br /> <br /> She also has <b>Matter 3</b>. Is that rank enough to craft the aforementioned vehicle?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your invaluable answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T05:09:59-07:00","id":1454439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1454425-crafting-a-vehicle-wonder#post1454425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello.<br /> Could it be an <b>Artifact</b> (meaning only awakened people could operate it and she would need <b>Prime 3</b>)?<br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> Is it necessary for that thing to be a <b>Talisman </b>(meaning it needs to have its own Arete and she would need <b>Prime 4</b>)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If she want's the plane itself to hold several effects, a Talisman it's the usual choice. But it could be both, or perhaps even <i>neither</i>.<br /> <br /> Since the Wright Brothers had already made a motor flyer, one could argue the magitech it's at the point where you could make a mundane motor plane, and enchant it's <i>engine</i>, so it uses <i>electricity </i>instead of other fuels (even if the Wright Brothers were Technocrats, one could argue that the fact that this was disclosed to the public - and the WAY it was disclosed - marks this as the point where it stops being pure magick. We're, literally, at &quot;the point on History where man invented flying machines&quot;, aren't we?)<br /> <br /> I think this could be a Trinket (meaning she would need Forces 3 and Matter 3), depending on how the effect works (the transformation &quot;electricity-&gt;kinetick&quot; would have to be continual)<br /> <br /> The plane being an artifact vs the motor being an artifact doesn't seemingly change anything in the rules (other than, maybe, allowing it to be done as a Trinket) - but it's still worth looking at because if you enchant only the motor, then the rest of the plane could be enhanced latter<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She also has <b>Matter 3</b>. Is that rank enough to craft the aforementioned vehicle? </div> </div> </div>Yesn't.<br /> <br /> It's not enough to make the vehicle just &quot;appear&quot; (Matter 4 would be needed). But if she's willing to actually &quot;make&quot; the plane by hand...<br /> <br /> In principle magick wouldn't be needed at all to make a carcase, that's just crafting. Even if we don't admit planes can exist without magick, the magick it's in the plane <i>flying</i>. No need of magick to make a complex &quot;sculpture&quot;, if you get what I mean.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 could could be used make the plane faster, cheaper,and a lot better than those first early planes. I don't know anything about engineering, so I can only speculate the advantages of making the parts to weight less or more, to be stronger and more flexible, to be of the material you want them to be regardless of it's rarity...at the very least, it should allow to make a stronger and more resistant plane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-07-2021, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T09:55:09-07:00","id":1454457,"title":"","content":"Well, she wants to do the plane by hand, so I guess Matter 4 is not necessary.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't see why it shouldnt be an Artifact (operated only by awakened people with that paradigm) with many effects cast on top of it, so I'll go with that.<br /> I guess the more effects you put on it, the more Quintessence you need to make it (or I'll play it like that if it's not the case).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T04:57:56-07:00","id":1454681,"title":"","content":"There's also a question of whether a Mage in 1910 could BUILD a plane or not. No magick, no arete rolls, just constructing it correctly using scientific principles.<br /> <br /> Some Mage players lean towards &quot;consensus defines reality&quot;, others lean towards &quot;reality exists, and consensus influences the ways in which reality can be influenced using Magick&quot;. Planes don't drop from the sky when you fly them over parts of the world where planes aren't believed in... or do they? Planes do crash...<br /> <br /> It's worth considering whether what the Mage is doing is Magick or not. If they're using Magick, then a Trinket might actually do. If they want it to fly using Forces then you'd want Prime and Forces to make an Artifact or Talisman. Either would make sense in character, just in the former case the Mage will say &quot;operating this flying machine requires an understanding of the mechanism, so I don't think a random civilian could fly it&quot; which does make a lot of sense for a plane regardless!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}